=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A thorough end-to-end investigation of the reported Office (192.168.3.x) → Internet Lab (128.168.0.x) connectivity failure found **no fault** at any layer.

**Affected component:** None identified. The symptom described in the helpdesk ticket — complete timeout from all office hosts to all Internet Lab machines — could not be reproduced or confirmed by any live evidence.

**Mechanism:** The complaint could not be confirmed because the path is fully functional. The forwarding fabric is a three-router RIP topology: office hosts on lan_office (192.168.3.0/24) reach the Internet Lab (128.168.0.0/16) via switch2 → router1 → router2 → switch5. All four office devices (office_pc, enquiry, exam_cell, tpo) were individually tested and reached every Internet Lab host (pc2–pc5) with 0% packet loss and ~1–2 ms RTT. The reverse direction (Internet Lab → Office) is equally clean.

**Localization:** No single device or interface was implicated. infra_sweep confirmed zero ACL/firewall rules, no mis-addressed hosts, and no gateway divergence across all 30 devices. l2_snapshot found no duplicate MACs. tc_snapshot found no traffic-shaping qdiscs. pressure_sweep found no resource contention. The RIP routing daemon (FRR ripd) is running correctly on all three routers, with complete routes installed in both directions. Journals are empty — no historical disruption traces exist.

**Root cause:** The reported connectivity failure between 192.168.3.x and 128.168.0.x is **unconfirmed**; no fault mechanism or historical trace was found in the live network, and all live probes succeeded.

**Fix:** No corrective action is required. If the users experience further timeout symptoms, capture the exact application/protocol (SSH, HTTP, ping) and source/destination at the time of failure to enable a targeted investigation.
=== END ===